# Quality gates

For every new feature, the agent **must** deliver:

## Tests

- **Unit tests — always** for new logic (Vitest, `*.test.ts` under `packages/`)
- Reference: `packages/core/src/prompts/index.test.ts`
- ESM imports with `.js`: `from "./index.js"` — except in `packages/angular`, where ng-packagr 20.3 needs extensionless relative imports
- **E2E (Playwright) — when the change touches a full user flow** (widget UI → host API route → response, e.g. search, cart, checkout, voice or camera overlays): add or extend a spec under `apps/demo-next/e2e` (and `apps/demo-angular/e2e` when the Angular widget is affected). Run with `pnpm test:e2e` after `pnpm build`; backends are mocked, no secrets needed

## Verification (all must pass)

```bash
pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm build
pnpm check:package   # after build (CI runs it every time)
pnpm check:consumer  # after build (CI runs it every time)
pnpm test:e2e        # when a user flow changed
```

- Zero ESLint errors (`eslint.config.mjs`, unused vars → prefix `_`)
- Zero TypeScript errors
- All tests green
- Green monorepo build (including both demo apps)

Do not finish work with a failing lint, typecheck, test, or build. CI runs the same steps in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (jobs `ci`, `e2e`, `angular-consumer`). The command list is generated from the root `package.json` scripts into `AGENTS.md` (`node scripts/print-commands.mjs --write`).

**Before every commit:** run the full verification command above and only commit when it passes. Never push a commit that would fail CI.
